From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LockPlus Vendor <vendor@localhost>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 21:00:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 09/11] W11: drop the unused Swift WireGuardAdapter and the
 wgSetConfig/wgGetConfig exports

LockPlus drives libwg-go through its own adapter (Tunnel/WireGuardGoBackend.swift); the upstream adapter was the
only caller. wgGetConfig returned the full UAPI dump including private_key and preshared_key, so removing both
exports shrinks the bridge's attack surface (Fable Simplification 3).
---
 Sources/WireGuardKit/WireGuardAdapter.swift | 487 --------------------
 Sources/WireGuardKitGo/api-apple-stats.go   |   2 +-
 Sources/WireGuardKitGo/api-apple.go         |  30 --
 Sources/WireGuardKitGo/wireguard.h          |   3 +-
 4 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 520 deletions(-)
 delete mode 100644 Sources/WireGuardKit/WireGuardAdapter.swift

